  "problem": "What is the $y$-intercept of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254588/assets/a213923ccd2b787862a41cce11e5f200a7d1879dcdc1dd6db9a7d6dd6ebc84de.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis, because $x=0$ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$",
